<section>
          <div class="container post-body">
            <a class="back-link" href="#blog" data-nav="blog">← Back to the blog</a>
            <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="lead-img" src="/images/img-034.avif" alt="Organic balloon garland arch" />
            <p>New to balloon decor? Here's a quick guide to the shapes and arrangements you'll see everywhere — and how to choose the right ones for your party.</p>
            <h2>The Main Arrangements</h2>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Organic garland</strong> — free-flowing clusters of different-sized balloons; the modern favorite</li>
              <li><strong>Classic arch</strong> — symmetrical arch over entrances and stages</li>
              <li><strong>Columns</strong> — vertical spiral stacks; great for framing doors and aisles</li>
              <li><strong>Bouquets</strong> — helium bunches tied to weights; perfect for tables and gifts</li>
              <li><strong>Centerpieces</strong> — smaller arrangements designed for table tops</li>
            </ul>
            <h2>Choosing Colors</h2>
            <p>Pick 2–3 colors max: one bold, one neutral, one metallic accent. Match them to your theme — school colors for graduation, pastels for baby showers, black &amp; gold for milestone birthdays.</p>
            <h2>DIY vs. Professional</h2>
            <p>Small bouquets are fun to DIY. But arches, walls and large installations? That's where professionals save you hours (and headaches). We handle design, delivery and setup across NJ &amp; NYC.</p>
